Player: Hey.. uhh...
Player: Are you the Atomon Expert Linos mentioned?
Andrew: May I ask who you are?
Player: I'm new here. Linos said I should learn about Atomons, like that weird thing I saw...
Andrew: Ahhh, Hydrubbie. The Hydrogen Atomon that wanders around here.
Andrew: It's hard to miss. Never causes trouble though.
Player: So... it's an Atomon?
Andrew: Correct! Atomons are living manifestations of the elements themselves.
Andrew: "Atomon" comes from "Atomic" and "Monster" — Atomic Monster.
Player: So Hydrubbie is... Hydrogen?
Andrew: Precisely! The lightest element there is.
Andrew: Don't let its size fool you. Hydrogen plays a very important role in chemistry.
Player: Chemistry...
Andrew: You'll be hearing that word often around here.
Andrew: If you're going to travel through Chemistria, you need to understand the elements and their Atomons.
Player: I guess I have a lot to learn...
Andrew: Indeed you do! But that's what I'm here for.
Player: How did this happen?
Andrew: What happened?
Player: This whole Atomon thing? How did elements become creatures?
Andrew: You're really clueless, huh? Even the children know what happened three years ago.
Player: What happened back then?
Andrew: It all started on that night....
Andrew: That night changed everything we knew about the elements.
Andrew: But before you can understand, you need to learn how to observe an Atomon carefully.
Player: Observe it?
Andrew: Yes. Start with Hydrubbie.
Andrew: Find three Hydrogen Atomons and observe them closely.
Player: What am I supposed to look for?
Andrew: Pay attention to what you can see and notice. Don't make assumptions.
Player: Alright. I'll observe three Hydrubbie.
Andrew: Good. Come back when you're finished, and we'll talk about what you discovered.

